<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51953" body-key="">
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καιετάεσσαν</span></b> 
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>full of hollows</i> or
				<i>abysses</i>, read by <i><span class="en">
				Zenod.
			</span></i> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κητώεσσαν</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.1
			</span></i>: but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὐρώτας καιετάεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					224
				</span></i>
			, is expld. by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλαμινθώδης</span>
			in Str.l.c.; cf. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καιέτα:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλαμίνθη</span> (
				Boeot.
			), <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καιέτας</span></b>  in <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κητώεσσαν</span>
			; gen. pl. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καιατῶν</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Anon.
			</span></i> Lond.<i><span class="en">
				36.57
			</span></i>.</div>
	</div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
